        prompts: {
          human: 'Welcome to Faro, the game that won the West. You see 13 card ranks on the layout. Place your chips on any rank. When the dealer draws two cardsâ€”first a Loser, then a Winnerâ€”you win if your card was the Winner. But if both cards match (a split), the house takes half your bet. Use the Case Keeper to track every card drawn. That knowledge is your edge.',
          ai: "Game: Faro (Pharaon). Banking game. Setup: Standard 52-card deck in dealing box. Soda card (first) discarded before play. Gameplay: Players bet on any of 13 ranks on layout, predicting 'Win' (second card drawn). Dealer exposes two cards per round: Loser (first), Winner (second). Outcomes: Bet on Loser card rank = House collects. Bet on Winner rank = 1:1 payout. Copper token inverts prediction to Loser. Splits (two identical ranks) = House takes 50% of all bets on that rank. Case Keeper tracks all drawn cards. Game continues until 3 cards remain (Hock). Calling the Turn: Players may bet order of final 3 cards at 4:1. House edge: ~1.4% from splits.",
        },
        scoring: {
          description: 'Betting outcomes determined by card draws. House profits from splits only.',
